 `thirdparty/spirv-headers`, `SPIRV_SKIP_TESTS=ON`, using `scripts/devshell.cmd`.
 The generator validates every Vulkan module for Vulkan 1.0 and preserves
 bindings and the 20-byte (16-byte scaled) push-constant interface.
+
+## Full fixed16 resolve (0201)
+
+`XE_RESOLVE_FIXED16` specializes the shared Canary full resolve helpers for
+EDRAM 16_16 and 16_16_16_16. Signed components use exact s5.10 (1/1024), with
+negative values below -1 preserved. Separate private pipelines keep all original
+non-fixed16 and gamma bytecodes intact. Raw integer fast copies are unchanged.
+The fixed16 sources reuse the SDK sample layout, scaled blocks and precise
+accumulation from 0199/0200. RGB565 continues to use the original pipelines.
+
+Run the same generator command with `--family fixed16` to regenerate these
+20 DXBC/SPIR-V resources. `fixed16_generated.json` pins all sources, tools,
+binary hashes and instruction statistics; `--verify` compares exact bytes.
+
+The unscaled 16/32/64/128bpp fixed16 resources preserve pinned compiler IR:
+only signed16 unpack scale and its source lower bound are regenerated. DXBC
+uses -32 as the exact minimum representable s5.10 value and refreshes its
+checksum; SPIR-V replaces the source FMax lower operand by the scaled value
+itself. Destination clamps and all other instructions are retained. The scalar
+R8 and scaled kernels are compiled from the specialized sources above.
+For fixed16 generation, build x360n_resolve_dxbc_checksum and pass
+--dxbc-checksum <x360n_resolve_dxbc_checksum.exe>. The manifest records the
+pinned input hashes and exact edited words; the resource test verifies that
+all remaining IR words and conversion instructions are unchanged.
